async def build_workflow() -> None:
    await GriptapeNodes.ahandle_request(RegisterLibraryFromFileRequest(library_name='Griptape Nodes Library', perform_discovery_if_not_found=True))
    context_manager = GriptapeNodes.ContextManager()
    if not context_manager.has_current_workflow():
        context_manager.push_workflow(file_path=__file__)
    # 1. We've collated all of the unique parameter values into a dictionary so that we do not have to duplicate them.
    #    This minimizes the size of the code, especially for large objects like serialized image files.
    # 2. We're using a prefix so that it's clear which Flow these values are associated with.
    # 3. The values are serialized using pickle, which is a binary format. This makes them harder to read, but makes
    #    them consistently save and load. It allows us to serialize complex objects like custom classes, which otherwise
    #    would be difficult to serialize.
    top_level_unique_values_dict = {'2323d74a-a6cf-4c5c-85f2-68daeacddf06': pickle.loads(b"\x80\x04\x95t\x18\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00Xm\x18\x00\x00# READ ME FIRST: Module 4, 1 Sources\n\n**Build it once: a node, then a library, then a template.** You describe a step your studio needs, and Griptape writes it as a node of your own. You package that node so a colleague can install it, and then you use it in a workflow anyone can run.\n\n## Where this fits\n\n**Before this:** **Module 3**, on the training site.\n\n**Next:** **Module 4, 2 Exercise 1: One custom node or widget**.\n\n## Not just the exercises\n- **Griptape's nodes are a starting set, not the limit.** If your studio needs a step that doesn't exist yet, describe it in plain words and Griptape writes the node for you. A node is a short Python file: what goes in, what it does, what comes out.\n- **Read a node before you load it.** A node's code runs inside Griptape with full access, like any script you install. Look at what *Write the Node* wrote first.\n- **A library is how a node travels.** It's a folder with your node in it, plus a label file. You've been installing Griptape's own libraries since day one; now you make one.\n- **A node can bring its own controls.** Beyond text boxes and dropdowns, a node can carry a widget: a small piece of interface made for one job, like picking a camera look visually instead of typing it, reordering shots by dragging them, or drawing on a picture. Griptape's post on custom widgets shows examples (link in the *Read* note). It lives in the same kind of library you build here: a JavaScript file, registered in the label file and named by a parameter on the node.\n- **A good template shows its choices.** The settings someone would change sit at the front (a Start Flow node), the results come out at the back (an End Flow node), and nothing important is hidden inside a node.\n- **A run without the window runs everything in the file.** So a template gets a workflow of its own, holding only what it needs. Module 5 runs one that way.\n\n## The canvas\n- **Start here** (this box): how to work through the module, plus videos, help pages, templates and the models used.\n- **Your Brief** (below, left): the picture description Exercise 1 starts from.\n- **The exercises** are their own workflows: **Module 4, 2 Exercise 1** to **Module 4, 4 Exercise 3** (File, Open). Each one reads the newest files this workflow saves.\n\n## Working through it\n**The results of a full run are already in:** every picture and video shows as soon as you open the template, with nothing to run. The steps say which node to press play on: do that only to make your own version, since running nodes yourself uses credits. Your own node is not in your Project yet: Exercise 1, step 3 writes it into the sandbox, so run that step before step 4.\n\n1. **Save the sources.** Press the play button on *Save Your Brief*: it saves into the sources folder, where every exercise looks.\n2. **Then the exercises.** Open **Module 4, 2 Exercise 1** (File, Open). Each exercise reads the newest files saved here, so run this workflow again whenever you change them.\n\nYour node isn't on the canvas when you start: Exercises 1 and 2 put it there.\n\n## Keys\n- **Tab** (or **Shift+A**) with the cursor over the canvas: add a node there. Type its app name, the first part of every node title here, such as **Save Text**.\n- **Ctrl+Enter**: run the selected node, and whatever it needs that has not run yet. **Ctrl+Shift+Enter**: run the whole workflow.\n- **Ctrl+S**: save. **F**: frame the selected node (with nothing selected, the whole workflow). **Space** (hold): pan the canvas. **Delete** or **Backspace**: remove the selected node or connection.\n- **Ctrl+Shift+S**: Save As, for the template in Exercise 3.\n- **Help, Keyboard Shortcuts** (**Shift+?**) lists the main keys. On a Mac, use **Cmd** where it says **Ctrl**.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- **Modules 1 to 3**, and someone on your team who is comfortable reading a short Python file.\n- **No files to download.** Griptape writes the node and its library file for you.\n- **A Griptape account with credits**, for *Write the Node*, *Write the Library File*, *Generate Shot Frame*, *Generate Plate* and *Check the Cut-Out*.\n- **The Advanced Media library**, for the cut-out in Exercise 3. Download **Grounding DINO base** (up to about 1.9 GB) and **SAM2 hiera tiny** (about 0.3 GB) in **Manage, Model Management**: type the model's ID (**IDEA-Research/grounding-dino-base**, **facebook/sam2-hiera-tiny**), pick it from the list, **Download**. On *Subject Matte* a downloaded model shows a tick, a missing one a download arrow. Already there if you did Module 2.\n- **An NVIDIA GPU** with about **2.5 GB of free video memory**, for that cut-out: G-DINO + SAM2 hiera tiny use about 2.2 GB. Without one, the cut-out runs on another GPU or on the CPU, which is slower.\n- **A second machine** with Griptape Nodes, for Exercise 2.\n- **Which models, and what they cost:** see the *Models* note on the right.\n\n## Where your files go\n- **Sources** go into the **sources/module\\_4** folder inside **{outputs}**. The exercises read the newest file there.\n- Pictures and text go into this Project's **outputs** folder: **{outputs}/images/module\\_4/exercise\\_1/** (a folder per shot, named by your node) and **exercise\\_3/**, and the text files under **{outputs}/text/module\\_4/**. The Project adds **\\_v001**, **\\_v002** ... so nothing is overwritten.\n- Your node and your library are code, so they go into this Project's own folder under their exact names: **sandbox\\_library/** and **studio\\_tools/**. Saving them again replaces them.\n\n## Good to know\n- **Keep one copy of your node loaded.** Delete the sandbox copy once the library is added.\n- **Changed the node?** Press play on *Save the Node* again, then **Refresh Libraries**. No restart needed.\n- **A workflow template is not a Project template.** A Project template decides where files are read and written (**Manage, Project Management, Create New Template**). Your workflow uses one.\n- **Griptape's own templates are flagged as templates.** The ready-made workflows that come with a library, like this one, are marked as templates in their file, so saving one makes your own copy and leaves the original alone. The template you save in Exercise 3 is a reusable workflow: anyone can open and run it, but Griptape does not list it among its templates.\x94."), '190b2105-b8ba-44f2-9208-9240b2212f40': pickle.loads(b'\x80\x04\x95$\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00X\x1d\x01\x00\x00# Watch\n- [Custom Node Development with AI Assisted Tools](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0y0kUZxM_ks): a node written with an AI coding assistant\n- [Easily Manage and Install Libraries in Griptape Nodes](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=29gJpg4LFN8): how a library gets onto a machine\x94.'), 'de3baa28-37f5-4dae-b2df-28f6bf07b496': pickle.loads(b"\x80\x04\x95\x9d\x06\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00X\x96\x06\x00\x00# Read\n- [Custom nodes: getting started](https://docs.griptapenodes.com/en/stable/development/custom_nodes/getting_started/): how a node is built, in about forty lines\n- [Parameters](https://docs.griptapenodes.com/en/stable/development/custom_nodes/parameters/): a node's inputs and outputs\n- [Authoring libraries](https://docs.griptapenodes.com/en/stable/development/custom_nodes/authoring_libraries/): the library's label file\n- [Custom widgets](https://docs.griptapenodes.com/en/stable/development/custom_nodes/custom_widgets/): your own controls on a node\n- [Custom widget components, with pictures](https://www.griptape.ai/blog/getting-started-with-custom-widget-components-in-foundry-griptape): a multi-shot video editor (from the Kling library) and a canvas for drawing on a picture (in the library template); colour palettes and mask painting are mentioned as ideas (Griptape, 6 May 2026)\n- [Libraries](https://docs.griptapenodes.com/en/stable/guides/libraries/): installing and adding libraries, and the sandbox\n- [Projects](https://docs.griptapenodes.com/en/stable/guides/projects/): Project templates and where files go\n\n## Griptape on GitHub\n- [Library template](https://github.com/griptape-ai/griptape-nodes-library-template): start a full library from here (**Use this template**)\n- [Node Development Guide](https://github.com/griptape-ai/griptape-nodes-node-development-guide): Griptape's own guide to writing nodes\n- [Nodes Directory](https://github.com/griptape-ai/griptape-nodes-directory): real libraries, each with an Add to Griptape Nodes link\n- [Testing library](https://github.com/griptape-ai/griptape-nodes-library-testing): nodes that check a workflow's results\x94."), '9df7c17c-e122-45ec-bd13-fd8dae8c52da': pickle.loads(b'\x80\x04\x959\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00X2\x01\x00\x00# Open\nTemplates in the app:\n- **Nano Banana Pro - Image Collage**: a real workflow with its input image at the front (Start Flow) and its results at the back (End Flow)\n\n## Next\nModule 5, Pipeline Integration: your template, run without the window and published into Nuke with a record of how it was made.\x94.'), '0689bda5-a595-4a54-9ea9-a3d976225dab': pickle.loads(b"\x80\x04\x95\x0c\x06\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00X\x05\x06\x00\x00# Models: why these\n\nEvery model here was picked so the whole module runs **the day you install Griptape Nodes**. They are a starting point, not a rule: you can swap any of them without touching the rest of the workflow.\n\n| Job | Model | Why this one | Cost, 1 Oct 2026 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Node and library file (Exercises 1 and 2) | Claude Opus 5.5 (Agent) | Writes code from a plain-words description | about $0.20 per file (estimate) |\n| Shot frame (Exercise 1) | GPT Image 1 Mini | Small, fast and cheap: just something to name and save | about $0.01 per image (estimate from OpenAI's token price) |\n| Plate (Exercise 3) | FLUX.2 [klein] 4B | Online, fixed seed, the same model as Modules 1 and 2 | $0.015 per 1536x1024 image (BFL list price: $0.014 for the first megapixel, $0.001 per extra one) |\n| Cut-out mask (Exercise 3) | Grounding DINO base + SAM2 hiera tiny | Finds the subject from a few words and makes the mask on your own machine; free to use (Apache 2.0) | free, runs on your machine |\n| Check (Exercise 3) | Claude Sonnet 5 (Describe Image) | Looks at the cut-out and writes a short quality note | about $0.01 or less per check (estimate) |\n\n**The whole workflow, run once (estimate, 1 Oct 2026):** about $0.10.\n\n**About the costs:** estimates in dollars. Griptape shows credit in dollars too: your balance at the top of the app, and each model's own price under **Manage Subscription**, **Pricing** (platform fees included). Prices change, so check your credit balance before and after a run to see what it really cost.\x94."), '0d86a2f5-4b75-41ed-b338-e03067657593': pickle.loads(b'\x80\x04\x95\x84\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x8c\x80A pelican rides a bicycle along a rainy seaside promenade at dusk. Warm streetlight, wet reflections on the pavement, wide shot.\x94.'), 'e31c536a-eb95-456e-96de-03dd4ea19ea4': pickle.loads(b'\x80\x04\x95a\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x8c1griptape_nodes.common.project_templates.situation\x94\x8c\x10BuiltInSituation\x94\x93\x94\x8c\x10save_node_output\x94\x85\x94R\x94.'), '014c71ca-84d9-48ac-8558-adaeab2fe944': pickle.loads(b'\x80\x04\x95#\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x8c\x1fsources/module_4/your_brief.txt\x94.'), '1e31f594-8643-43dc-9520-0880656dabfe': pickle.loads(b'\x80\x04\x95g\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x8cc**Read this first.** What the workflow does, how to run it, what you need, and where to learn more.\x94.'), 'f81b8911-9174-4aca-b3f7-6fbd158bd234': pickle.loads(b'\x80\x04\x95/\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x8c+Replace it with a brief from your own show.\x94.')}
